SUMMARY:Econometrics – Dakyung Seong (University of Sydney) – Spillover
  Effects in Fuzzy Regression Discontinuity Design
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Dakyung Seong: “Spillover Effects in Fuzzy Regression Discont
 inuity Design”\nhttps://sites.google.com/view/dkseong/\n\nZoom: https://
 unimelb.zoom.us/j/85966225829?pwd=g6hOdHyvYB0qta0aFzGbWOgczJ1Qzr.1\n\nGoog
 le Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nThis pape
 r studies treatment spillovers in fuzzy regression discontinuity (RD) desi
 gns with socially interacting units\, such as couples\, friends\, and neig
 hbors. Because an individual's treatment take-up may respond to both their
  own and their peer's treatment assignments\, standard fuzzy RD identifica
 tion strategies are generally invalid in this setup. This paper establishe
 s new identification results for direct\, indirect\, and social-interactio
 n local average treatment effects under alternative restrictions on joint 
 compliance behavior. We also develop local-polynomial estimators and bias-
 corrected inference procedures and examine their finite-sample performance
  via Monte Carlo simulations. The proposed identification and estimation a
 pproaches are applied to study the impact of retirement on health behavior
 s. The estimates suggest that spousal retirement significantly reduces dri
 nks per drinking day among men whose spouses belong to certain compliance 
 groups.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/85966225829?pwd=g6hOdHyvYB0qta0aFzGbWOgczJ1Qz
 r.1
END:VEVENT
